  "regression_evidence": [
    "New experiments preserve the exact source and matcher set, inherit supported baselines, retain adopted baseline ancestry, and reset learner/cohort/exposure state without copying prior samples.",
    "Existing native sessions retain their experiment and arm across revisions and restart. Explicit empty snapshots do not acquire later blocks; legacy baseline/adoption records resolve the original experiment.",
    "Incomplete capture may retain an inherited baseline but cannot enroll a trial, including after coverage becomes available in an already admitted session.",
    "A changed control generation during live dependency resolution rejects admission before enrollment, rather than mixing current and archived route snapshots.",
    "An archived exploring experiment can retain favorable statistics but cannot newly adopt or enroll. Archived canonical corrections invalidate prepared evidence and can withdraw the earlier adoption and its descendants.",
    "Successive ancestor withdrawals resolve the last supported baseline. A second withdrawal advances even an already rolled-back descendant revision, invalidating a block that declared a dependency on it.",
    "Assembled local HTTP execution verifies the actual model used by old and new sessions, and their return to the configured baseline after archived adoption withdrawal.",
    "The local IPC/TUI flow preserves matcher identity, edits candidate routes, previews live baselines, rebases changed route contracts, rejects later reloads, and displays per-version historical evidence.",
    "Registration retries return the original experiment receipt after a later revision exists, without changing the mode or creating another revision. TUI evidence reconciliation targets the displayed experiment ID."
  ],
